  "narrative": "The new evidence tests whether the four accepted associations are context-dependent or technically driven. For WRN, the adenocarcinoma interaction H17 and high-Cas9 interaction H29 are near zero with intervals containing zero and spanning clinically relevant values; they do not show that MSI-high dependency is confined to adenocarcinoma or weaker/stronger in high-Cas9 screens. The mutation-burden interaction H24 is analytically invalid because the exposed complement cell is empty: MSI-high samples are essentially all above the median mutation-burden cut-point, so this comparison cannot estimate modification. For NFE2L2 and SMARCA2, the high-Cas9 interactions H30/H31 and lineage interactions H39/H40 are small and inconclusive; they do not accept context-specific amplification or attenuation, but they also do not undermine the very large main associations. The EGFR and ERBB2 context analyses H21, H34, and H35 remain unresolved at best: EGFR amplification has weak positive trends in adenocarcinoma and KRAS-wildtype strata, but the intervals include zero and the earlier main-effect validation was discordant; ERBB2 remains essentially null after excluding EGFR-amplified samples. KRAS dependency PIK3CA interaction H36 is not supported. The one biologically interesting unresolved interaction is H37: TP53 loss may affect USP7 dependency more strongly in KEAP1-loss cells, signed estimate +0.122, but the 95% interval crosses zero and is wide, so it cannot be accepted. I request validation for H13 because it is the strongest data-driven reversal (KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency) and independent confirmation would most reduce the risk of accepting a reversed false lead. I do not request validation for H20 now; it was pre-registered and biologically coherent, and its robustness interactions are null rather than contradictory. All conclusions remain dataset-specific associations, not causal effects or generalizable biological claims.",
  "research_notes": "Round-3 appraise update. Signed contrasts are already oriented to the claim. More negative raw dependency means stronger dependency. Accepted dataset-specific associations remain: H10 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency, signed +0.790 [0.760,0.819]; H11 TP53-loss -> weaker USP7 dependency, signed +0.396 [0.325,0.467]; H13 KEAP1-loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency, signed +0.796 [0.776,0.816], reversed from original anticipated direction and now pending independent validation; H20 SMARCA4-loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency, signed +0.784 [0.765,0.803]. H20 investigation closed as accepted; H13 remains active pending validation. New null/inconclusive robustness and context tests: WRN adenocarcinoma interaction H17; WRN high-Cas9 interaction H29; NFE2L2 high-Cas9 H30 and lineage H39; SMARCA2 high-Cas9 H31 and lineage H40; EGFR adenocarcinoma H21; EGFR KRAS-wildtype H34; ERBB2 EGFR-negative H35; KRAS PIK3CA interaction H36. H24 invalid due empty cell: all MSI-high appear above median mutation burden, so no independent interaction contrast is estimable. EGFR amplification remains the least stable RTK signal: discovery, validation, and context estimates are inconsistent or borderline. USP7 TP53-loss by KEAP1-loss interaction H37 is unresolved and remains active because the point estimate is moderately large despite a wide interval. Next analyze should prioritize untested broad outcome probes H32 KIF18A by RB1 loss and H33 TMED10 by ERBB2 amplification, then assess H13 validation when it arrives. Avoid further low-powered interaction follow-up unless it clarifies accepted effects or a pre-registered biologically coherent hypothesis."
}

