  "narrative": "The new discovery results materially strengthen the two main accepted but not yet independently validated associations, while also refuting several new predictor hypotheses. For H20, the SMARCA4-loss SMARCA2 dependency effect remains enormous in both ARID1A-loss cells (H45, signed +0.814, interval +0.767 to +0.862) and ARID1A-intact cells (H46, +0.777, +0.756 to +0.798), and in Avana-library screens (H63, +0.781, +0.760 to +0.802). Because positive signed values for direction -1 claims correspond to more negative dependency scores and therefore stronger dependency, these estimates support SMARCA4-loss being associated with stronger SMARCA2 dependency within the supplied dataset. They are not held-out independent validation because they reuse discovery observations, but they are strong within-data consistency checks that reduce the likelihood that the main H20 association is driven by ARID1A co-loss or by non-Avana library screens. I accept H45, H46, and H63 as dataset-specific subgroup robustness associations and close those subgroup investigations; I keep H20 active for possible validation. For H11, the TP53-loss USP7 effect is also robust: it is present in KEAP1-loss cells (H47, +0.493, +0.351 to +0.635), KEAP1-intact cells (H48, +0.370, +0.289 to +0.452), and Avana-library screens (H64, +0.405, +0.330 to +0.479). These are direction +1 claims, so positive signed values mean weaker USP7 dependency with TP53 loss. H37 remains rejected because the KEAP1-loss interaction estimate is wide and includes zero, while the stratified main effects show the TP53-loss association in both KEAP1 strata; this is a claim-level rejection of the specific interaction hypothesis, not proof that no interaction exists. I request independent validation for H11 because it is an accepted association of scientifically important but more moderate magnitude than H20, it has no held-out validation yet, and the subgroup evidence is not independent. H20 remains a later validation priority because its effects are extremely large and internally robust, whereas H11 is the more consequential current uncertainty. The new null results are also informative. BRCA2 loss does not support stronger WRN dependency overall (H53) or in MSI-negative cells (H54), so the accepted MSI-high WRN association does not appear to be explained by BRCA2 loss or an independent BRCA2 replication-stress effect. CDKN2A loss does not support weaker USP7 dependency (H58), and RB1 loss does not support stronger KIF18A dependency (H32). The TMED10 specificity probes for TP53 loss (H59) and SMARCA4 loss (H60) are near null, supporting outcome specificity of the accepted predictors rather than a broad global screen artifact. I also close H8 and H4 as unsupported main-effect claims: TP53 loss does not show a meaningful MDM2 effect, and ERBB2 amplification does not show a meaningful ERBB2 dependency effect. All conclusions remain associations in this supplied dataset; none establishes causality or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Round-4 appraise update. Validation now requested for H11 (TP53-loss -> weaker USP7). H20 remains accepted and active as next validation priority. New robustness evidence: H45/H46/H63 strongly support H20; H47/H48/H64 strongly support H11. H37 interaction rejected; direct TP53-loss USP7 effects exist in both KEAP1-loss and KEAP1-intact strata. Null/refuted: H32 RB1->KIF18A, H53/H54 BRCA2->WRN, H58 CDKN2A->USP7, H59/H60 TMED10 specificity, H8 TP53->MDM2, H4 ERBB2 amplification->ERBB2. Accepted H10, H13 remain validated. Next analysis: prioritize H20 validation after H11 validation returns; keep broad probes H51/H52/H55/H56/H57 active if useful; defer redundant accepted-effect context probes H41-H44, H49/H50, H61/H62, and broad H33/H38 unless new rationale appears. All findings are supplied-dataset associations, not causal or generalizable.",
