h was tested against DHX9 to determine whether the accepted MSI-high WRN effect is helicase/repair-general or more WRN-specific. SMARCA4 loss was tested against POLR2A to assess whether the SMARCA2 effect extends to broad transcription machinery or remains chromatin/paralog specific. ARID1A loss was tested within SMARCA4-loss cells to examine residual co-dependency beyond the dominant SMARCA4-loss association. PIK3CA mutation was tested against STAT3 to add pathway-diverse coverage across kinase/inflammatory signaling outcomes.\n\nAll new claims remain dataset-specific associations. Acceptance would require a signed estimate and interval that are scientifically meaningful under the approximate 10% relative-difference criterion, while independent held-out validation would be needed to assess stability and reduce the possibility that a discovery association is context-specific to the supplied data split."
