  "narrative": "I assessed all newly delivered discovery evidence with the same approximate benchmark: about 0.1 absolute dependency-score difference is meaningful, while the returned estimates are already signed to the claim direction. For direction -1 claims, positive means stronger dependency; for direction +1 claims, positive means weaker dependency.  The CDKN2A-MDM2 decomposition was the main priority. In TP53-intact, MTAP-loss cells, CDKN2A loss was associated with stronger MDM2 dependency: H78 signed +0.162 (95% +0.070 to +0.255). This is suggestive, but the lower confidence bound is below the 0.1 benchmark and the subgroup estimate was generated after many secondary tests. I therefore leave H78 unresolved but active. More informative for avoiding MTAP-proxy confounding is H79, the CDKN2A effect among TP53-intact, MTAP-intact cells: signed +0.106 (95% +0.063 to +0.150). The direction and point estimate support persistence when MTAP is not lost, but the interval also crosses the 0.1 importance threshold. I therefore leave H79 unresolved. H82 showed a similar estimate in TP53-intact low-9p21 cells: signed +0.112 (95% +0.062 to +0.162), but low-9p21 is highly entangled with CDKN2A deletion itself and the lower bound is below 0.1, so H82 remains unresolved. H83 tested whether low-9p21 modifies the CDKN2A-MDM2 association: interaction signed -0.061 (95% -0.222 to +0.100). This provides no evidence of a meaningful interaction, so I reject and close H83. H81 could not be assessed because the non-low-9p21/TP53-intact CDKN2A-loss cell had only one observation, R69; I leave it unresolved and close that impossible stratified analysis rather than interpret sparse cells.  MTAP as an independent driver was much less compelling. H80, the main MTAP-loss effect on MDM2 in TP53-intact cells, was small and near null: signed +0.024 (95% -0.005 to +0.054). H84, MTAP loss among TP53-intact CDKN2A-intact cells, was near null: signed +0.009 (95% -0.015 to +0.033). H85 and H86, MTAP 