  "narrative": "H11 has now received its scheduled independent validation response. For direction +1, the positive signed validation estimate +0.448 (independent 95% +0.347 to +0.549) means TP53-loss cells have higher, less negative USP7 dependency scores, i.e., weaker USP7 dependency. This closely supports the discovery estimate +0.396 (95% +0.325 to +0.467) and is far above the approximate 0.1 benchmark. I therefore accept H11 as a strong dataset-specific association and close it. H66 tests MTAP loss as a predictor of weaker USP7 dependency. Its validation is small and imprecise: signed +0.022 (independent 95% -0.038 to +0.083), far below the importance benchmark and crossing zero; the discovery result was also near null and opposite in direction. I keep H66 rejected and closed.  The main new result is H77, the reversed CDKN2A-MDM2 claim in TP53-intact cells. H77 has direction -1, so positive signed estimates mean CDKN2A loss is associated with more negative MDM2 dependency scores, i.e., stronger MDM2 dependency. Discovery was +0.119 (95% +0.079 to +0.158) and independent validation was +0.129 (independent 95% +0.073 to +0.185). The replicated point estimates are around 0.12-0.13, about half an SD of the MDM2 dependency distribution, and the independent interval excludes zero under the stringent validation alpha. The exact size remains somewhat uncertain because the lower confidence bounds fall below 0.1, so I characterize this as a moderate, not large, dataset-specific association. I accept H77 and close the primary investigation. The MTAP decomposition supports, but does not separately warrant accepting, a subgroup claim: MTAP main effects were small or null (H80, H84-H86), the low-9p21 interaction was not supported (H83), and the MTAP-intact CDKN2A contrast H79 was directionally consistent but still exploratory. I therefore close H78/H79/H82 as unresolved supportive stratum analyses rather than accept them independently.  I also cleared several long-deferred claims whose evidence is unambiguously below the approximate scientific-importance benchmark. KRAS mutation main effect H1, serum-condition effect H12, EGFR amplification effect in KRAS-wild-type H34, ERBB2 amplification effect in EGFR-non-amplified H35, KRAS-Pik3ca interaction H36, and several small EGFR/KRAS/NFE2L2/SMARCA2/USP7 interactions (H14, H16, H17, H18, H19, H21, H22, H28, H29, H30, H31, H39, H40) have estimates near zero with upper confidence bounds at or below about 0.1 or otherwise no support for the registered direction. I reject and close those. The next informative work is to test context specificity of the new moderate CDKN2A-MDM2 association: TP53-intact adenocarcinoma, TP53-intact Avana-library cells, and a formal MTAP interaction probe. In parallel, the existing untested probes for accepted axes (H90, H91) and outcome-specific probes for TMED10, STAT3, RIT1, and POLR2A remain reasonable low-priority follow-ups.",
